course: dictionary
lesson: 11472
title: Words that speak up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An advocate is someone who speaks up for an idea or for other people. To advocate something is to publicly support it, which means you say out loud that you are for it. You can use it as a noun or a verb: «Mia is an advocate for animal rights.» and «The council advocates more bike lanes.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mia spoke at the meeting, asked for more parks, and wanted every dog to have a safe place to run.» Words like spoke, asked and wanted show that an advocate is someone who speaks up and works for a cause. Swap in your meaning: "Mia is someone who speaks up for animal rights" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Be careful: the word has a special meaning in law. In Scotland, «The advocate stood up in court to speak for Sam» means a type of lawyer who speaks for a person in court. Context tells you which meaning is used. Ask yourself whether the sentence is about a cause or about a court.
explain: Three phrases to learn: advocate for means to support a person or cause, as in «an advocate for clean rivers». An advocate of means a believer in an idea, as in «an advocate of reading every day». Devil's advocate means arguing the other side on purpose to test an idea, even if you do not really believe it.
fact: An advocate is a person who speaks up for an idea or for other people.
fact: To advocate something means to publicly support it or speak in favour of it.
fact: In Scotland, an advocate is a lawyer who speaks for someone in court.
fact: «Advocate for» means to support a person or cause, and «an advocate of» means a believer in an idea.
fact: «Devil's advocate» means arguing the other side on purpose to test an idea.
exercise: «Mia is an advocate for animal rights.» What is an advocate here? | A kind of animal | *A person who speaks up for an idea | A place where animals live | A type of food
exercise: «The school council advocates more bike racks.» What does advocates mean? | Hides | *Publicly supports | Removes | Counts
exercise: «In court, the advocate spoke for Sam.» In this sentence, what kind of person is an advocate? | *A lawyer who speaks for someone in court | A police officer | A judge who listens | A teacher who marks tests
test: Which phrase means arguing the other side on purpose to test an idea? | Advocate for | Bike racks | *Devil's advocate | An advocate of
test: Which word in «The club advocated cleaner rivers» means publicly supported? | rivers | club | *advocated | cleaner
exam: Which sentence uses advocate to mean a lawyer? | *«The advocate argued Ben's case in the court in Glasgow.» | «She is an advocate for clean air.» | «He advocated a longer lunch break.»
